<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel traffic disrupted, though few heed strike call.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel traffic disrupted, though few heed strike call.</headline>
<dateline>COQUELLES, France</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tourist traffic on the rail line under the English Channel was disrupted Wednesday by striking pickets blocking toll gates, although few workers heeded a strike call at the British-French Eurotunnel.</p>
<p>Freight traffic and passenger trains were not affected by the picketing, which was the first major action by the Eurotunnel unions.</p>
<p>The French unions had called for a job action for Wednesday afternoon through the evening. The unions are demanding better working conditions and accuse management of ignoring grievances over salaries and working hours.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel management declined to comment.</p>
</text>
